{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9188-1","published":"2026-11-23T19:44:23Z","modified":"2026-11-24T15:01:51.159118458Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-118669","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-49264","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-49265","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-49272"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-118669","CVE-2026-49264","CVE-2026-49265","CVE-2026-49272","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-118669","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-49264","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-49265","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-49272"],"summary":"python-oauthlib vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that OAuthLib incorrectly handled JSONP callback\nparameters in the token revocation endpoint. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to execute arbitrary code in a client\napplication. (CVE-2026-49264)\n\nElvin Latifli discovered that OAuthLib incorrectly compared PKCE code\nverifiers, using a comparison that was not constant-time. A remote\nattacker could possibly use this issue to obtain access tokens,\nresulting in an account takeover. This issue only affected Ubuntu 26.10,\nUbuntu 26.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04\nLTS. (CVE-2026-49265)\n\nStrick Sheng discovered that OAuthLib incorrectly validated the client\nidentity. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to obtain\ntokens authorized under another client, bypassing token authorization.\n(CVE-2026-118669)\n\nKyle Hekhuis discovered that OAuthLib incorrectly validated device codes\nin the device authorization workflow. A remote attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to obtain a token without completing device authorization.\nThis issue only affected Ubuntu 26.10 and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-49272)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python-oauthlib","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/python-oauthlib?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.0.3-1ubuntu0.1~esm1"}]}],"versions":["1.0.0-1","1.0.3-1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: 